With speculations surrounding his future, Rohit Sharma smashed an 84-ball century - his 34th in ODI - to light up the iconic Lord’s cricket ground in London, driving India’s chase of 388 in the series decider against England on Sunday. Imagine the backdrop. A few people had written him off, while reports claimed Rohit could be playing his last game for India today. Form had deserted him in the first two matches, as scores of 11 and 26 suggest.
